From 7d6586c04b33457be1acd8189e57f08e5d8a8479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:24:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban schema owner: sync DDL in the at-par
 reference; never create a missing board; CLI one-line refusal

Follow-ups to PR #2019 (only a home's installed core migrates its board) from exact-head review 5889519484
(card t_01a1d473f87f6999), card t_01a1d47a6e38a25b.

1. The at-par reference missed the sync schema. `_reference_schema` replayed only
   `kanban_db_connect.apply_schema_steps`, while `register_without_install` marks an attached board synced.
   If main adds a sync table/column the installed core lacks, a non-installed checkout opened read-write
   with sync live and could fail later with a raw "no such column". Now `kanban_db_sync.apply_sync_schema_steps`
   is the one list of sync DDL steps (`install_or_remove` runs it), and when the board would be registered
   synced (`live_without_install`, the predicate `register_without_install` already used) the reference
   includes it. A synced board lacking a sync column this core declares opens read-only and refuses writes
   with BoardSchemaNotOwned naming the column.
2. A non-installed checkout connecting to a board file that does not exist yet left a 4096-byte empty
   kanban.db (plus sidecars). `connect`/`init_db` now call `refuse_missing_board` before mkdir/open: in a
   home with an installed core that is not this one, a missing board raises BoardSchemaNotOwned and
   nothing is created.
3. `hermes kanban` printed BoardSchemaNotOwned as a full traceback (live check on worker-4, evidence
   t_01a1d3fb5bab541f/run9). `kanban_command` now prints its one-line message to stderr and exits 1, for
   both init_db and the action handler.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_schema_owner.py, 19 pass): 4 new cases fail on origin/main
(sync reference == synced connect; fake sync column -> BoardSchemaNotOwned with triggers/columns unchanged;
missing board not created; CLI one line, rc 1); a sync-off guard case shows the sync DDL is not required
there. Neighbouring suites (13 files touching the schema owner / sync install, 450 tests; 8 files with an
installed-core home layout, 904 tests) pass. scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
